<description>
Closes #6476

Adds `-outboundbind=<addr>` to set the source address of outgoing clearnet
connections, one per address family. It is separate from `-bind`; without it,
outbound follows the OS routing table as before.

- The command line wins over the config file, as for other options.
- Clearnet only: Tor and I2P use their own transport, CJDNS is direct but not
  IPv4/IPv6, and a proxy leaves the option inert for that family (with a
  startup warning).
- The effective address per family is trial-bound at startup, like `-bind` via
  `BindListenPort`; a port, the wildcard, or a non-clearnet value is rejected. A
  failed bind at connect time aborts the connection, with no fallback.

Functional and unit tests cover both families, the startup rejections, and the
bind-before-connect path.

Based on vasild's approach in
https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/6476#issuecomment-1666472338.
</description>

<commits>
ad220492e1 net: add -outboundbind option for outgoing source address

Add -outboundbind=<addr> to set the source address of outgoing
clearnet connections, one per address family, for multi-homed hosts.
It is separate from -bind (listening only); without it, outbound
follows the OS routing table as before.

- The command line wins over the config file, as for other options.
- Only clearnet is bound: Tor and I2P use their own transport, and
  CJDNS is direct but not IPv4/IPv6, so all three are unaffected. A
  proxy configured for a family leaves the option inert, with a
  startup warning.
- A port, the wildcard, or a non-clearnet value is rejected at
  startup; the effective address per family is trial-bound, as -bind
  does via BindListenPort, so a command-line value can override a
  stale config-file one.
- A failed bind at connect time aborts the connection, with no
  fallback, and is not counted against the peer in addrman, as proxy
  failures are not. Where available, IP_BIND_ADDRESS_NO_PORT keeps
  source port selection at connect() time. Use -nooutboundbind to
  disable the option.

Based on vasild's 2023 sketch:
https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/6476#issuecomment-1666472338

Closes #6476

9fae34c76f test: add tests for outbound bind address selection

Unit tests: Init() stores the source per address family (an unset
family stays unset); SelectOutboundBind() returns the per-family
source and nothing for a non-clearnet (Tor/I2P/CJDNS) target;
IsAddrBindable() reports whether an address can be bound; and
ConnectDirectly() binds the socket before connecting (recording mock
that accepts only the exact per-family sockaddr length), does not
bind without a source, aborts on a failed bind, and reports local
bind failures through bind_failed.

Functional test: outgoing connections originate from the -outboundbind
address for both families, with a loopback destination so the observed
source differs from it. Also checks command-line-over-config override,
the family-specific proxy warning (with an onion-only negative case),
and startup rejection of an unassigned address, a port, the wildcard,
a Tor address, and a CJDNS address. Skipped only when binding the CI
source addresses themselves fails.

5baa78a79c doc: add release notes for -outboundbind
</commits>

